From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:36:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WNM: Pass the space left in the BSS TM Request buffer to mbo_add_ie()

wnm_send_bss_tm_req() passes buf + sizeof(buf) - pos as the space left
for the MBO element. buf is a pointer, so the difference is negative and
converts to a size_t near SIZE_MAX. The length check in mbo_add_ie()
thus never fails.

Pass the space that is left in the allocation. No write went past the
buffer, because the frame without the Neighbor Report elements and the
MBO attributes takes at most 305 of the 1000 octets that the allocation
adds for it.

Fixes: c0e2a172a768 ("hostapd: Add MBO IE to BSS Transition Management Request frame")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
@@ -963,6 +963,7 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 			const u8 *mbo_attrs, size_t mbo_len)
 {
 	u8 *buf, *pos;
+	size_t buf_len;
 	struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt;
 	size_t url_len;
 	const u8 *own_addr = wnm_ap_get_own_addr(hapd, sta);
@@ -972,7 +973,8 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 		   " req_mode=0x%x disassoc_timer=%d valid_int=0x%x dialog_token=%u",
 		   MAC2STR(sta->addr), req_mode, disassoc_timer, valid_int,
 		   dialog_token);
-	buf = os_zalloc(1000 + nei_rep_len + mbo_len);
+	buf_len = 1000 + nei_rep_len + mbo_len;
+	buf = os_zalloc(buf_len);
 	if (buf == NULL)
 		return -1;
 	mgmt = (struct ieee80211_mgmt *) buf;
@@ -1016,7 +1018,7 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 	}
 
 	if (mbo_len > 0) {
-		pos += mbo_add_ie(pos, buf + sizeof(buf) - pos, mbo_attrs,
+		pos += mbo_add_ie(pos, buf + buf_len - pos, mbo_attrs,
 				  mbo_len);
 	}
 
